          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Protagoras's Background</strong><br>\nProtagoras was a pre-Socratic Greek philosopher, born around 490 BCE in Abdera, Thrace. He is often recognized as one of the most prominent figures in the sophistic movement, which was a group of itinerant teachers who traveled around Greece educating people in exchange for money. Protagoras's teaching focused on rhetoric and the ability to argue both sides of a case, an essential skill in the democratic processes of ancient Athens.</p>\n\n<p><strong>His Philosophical Standpoint</strong><br>\nProtagoras is famous for his saying, \"Man is the measure of all things,\" which implies that there is no absolute truth, only that which individuals deem to be the truth based on their own perception. This perspective laid the groundwork for what we know as relativism in philosophy. Protagoras believed that because perceptions vary from person to person, all beliefs and values hold truth depending on one's individual perspective.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Sophism</strong><br>\nProtagoras's role as a sophist was significant; he developed a method of argumentation that emphasized the relativity of truth and the necessity of debate. He taught his students how to make weak arguments stronger, a skill that was highly valued in Athenian society for its practical use in law courts and political life. This teaching method reflected the democratic ideals of ancient Athens, where public debate and persuasion were key to civic participation.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
